CPU Monitoring using PSUTIL

Aim

To monitor CPU functions using the psutil library in Raspberry Pi.

Requirements

- Raspberry Pi
- Python 3
- psutil library

Description

The psutil library is used to check CPU performance.

- "psutil.cpu_percent(interval=1)" checks CPU usage percentage.
- "psutil.cpu_count()" checks the number of CPU cores.

Execution

Run the program using:

"python3 psutil_cpu.py"

Output

Displays CPU usage percentage and number of CPU cores.

Conclusion

CPU functions are successfully checked using the psutil library.
